{
  "dom_id": "step-q96559",
  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Given that $X$ is a random variable such that $X∼U[-7,3],$ find $\\text{SD}[X].$ Round your answer to three decimal places.",
  "worked_solution": "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-7$ and $b=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(3-(-7))^{2}}{12}=\\frac{100}{12}=\\frac{25}{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{3}}=\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{3}≈2.887.\n$$",
